{"ClientSettings":{"Pn":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"P"},"Sc":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"H"},"Qz":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"T"},"Ap":true,"Mute":true,"Lad":"2026-07-12T00:00:00Z","Iotd":0,"Gwb":0,"Tns":0,"Dft":null,"Mvs":0,"Flt":0,"Imp":1,"Tobn":0},"MediaContents":[{"ImageContent":{"Description":"If you're looking for Maine in the United States at its most untamed, this is it. Katahdin Woods and Waters National Monument spans more than 350 square kilometres of rugged North Woods wilderness, where still ponds reflect the sky and dense forests seem to absorb every sound.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.KatahdinWWNM_EN-IN8091413320_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.KatahdinWWNM_EN-IN8091413320_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Where the forest swallows sound","Title":"Katahdin Woods and Waters National Monument, Maine, United States","Copyright":"© Cavan Images/Offset/Shutterstock","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/46.156481,-68.717751/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&shading=flat&pp=46.156481,-68.717751;S9;Katahdin Woods and Waters National Monument, Maine, United States&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260712_KatahdinWWNM\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Katahdin+Woods+and+Waters+National+Monument&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260711_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260712_KatahdinWWNM"},"Ssd":"20260712","Name":"KatahdinWWNM","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"8091413320","FullDateString":"12 Jul, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"In France, Port de Saint-Goustan lies just below Auray's upper town, where a narrow tidal inlet along the Auray River opens towards the Gulf of Morbihan. The harbour sits along the Auray River, also known locally as the Loc’h, creating its sheltered, storybook setting. In the 13th century, the Dukes of Brittany built a bridge, a port and a castle here; the fortress has long since disappeared, but cobbled quays, winding lanes and timber-framed houses still line the waterfront.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.AurayBrittany_EN-IN7972438884_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.AurayBrittany_EN-IN7972438884_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Where Brittany meets the tide","Title":"Port de Saint-Goustan, Auray, Brittany, France","Copyright":"© Rolf E. Staerk/Shutterstock","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/47.664311,-2.977482/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&shading=flat&pp=47.664311,-2.977482;S9;Port de Saint-Goustan, Auray, France&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260711_AurayBrittany\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Auray+Saint-Goustan+France&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260710_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260711_AurayBrittany"},"Ssd":"20260711","Name":"AurayBrittany","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"7972438884","FullDateString":"11 Jul, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Land or sea? In Victoria, you don't have to choose. This southeastern Australian state proves that the best adventures come with a little of both.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.VictoriaBeach_EN-IN4783068086_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.VictoriaBeach_EN-IN4783068086_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"The land of moving shorelines","Title":"Aerial view of land and ocean, Victoria, Australia","Copyright":"© Nearmap/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/-36.850086,144.304291/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&shading=flat&pp=-36.850086,144.304291;S9;Victoria, Australia&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260710_VictoriaBeach\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Victoria+Australia&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260709_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260710_VictoriaBeach"},"Ssd":"20260710","Name":"VictoriaBeach","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"4783068086","FullDateString":"10 Jul, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Sunlight breaks through drifting clouds and settles on the terraced slopes of Sapa, where rice fields spill down the mountainsides in sweeping layers like a living staircase. Nestled in Vietnam's Lào Cai Province, this highland region is shaped as much by human endeavour as by nature. For centuries, farmers from ethnic communities such as the Hmong have carved and maintained these terraces, channelling water across steep hillsides to nourish each growing season.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.SapaVietnam_EN-IN2086925801_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.SapaVietnam_EN-IN2086925801_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Tradition in every step","Title":"Rice fields at Sapa, Lào Cai, Vietnam","Copyright":"© Anujak Jaimook/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/22.374456,103.842076/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&shading=flat&pp=22.374456,103.842076;S9;Sapa, Lào Cai, Vietnam&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260709_SapaVietnam\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Lao+Cai+Vietnam&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260708_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260709_SapaVietnam"},"Ssd":"20260709","Name":"SapaVietnam","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"2086925801","FullDateString":"9 Jul, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Set in Guatemala's western highlands, Lake Atitlán fills a vast volcanic caldera. Its deep blue waters are framed by steep crater walls and the cone-shaped volcanoes Atitlán, Tolimán and San Pedro. Wooden piers stretch into the still lake, emphasising the contrast between its calm surface and the rugged terrain shaped by volcanic activity.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.LakeAtitlan_EN-IN1783282765_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.LakeAtitlan_EN-IN1783282765_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Echoes of a volcanic past","Title":"Lake Atitlán, Guatemala","Copyright":"© shayes17/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/14.702858,-91.194628/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&shading=flat&pp=14.702858,-91.194628;S9;Lake Atitlán, Sololá, Guatemala&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260708_LakeAtitlan\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Lake+Atitlan+Guatemala&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260707_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260708_LakeAtitlan"},"Ssd":"20260708","Name":"LakeAtitlan","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"1783282765","FullDateString":"8 Jul, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"A bill like a multitool and plumage full of colour—the plate-billed mountain toucan is one of the Andes' most distinctive birds. It lives in the humid mountain forests of Ecuador and southwestern Colombia, perfectly adapted to life high in the canopy.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.MountainToucanOrchids_EN-IN1662413935_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.MountainToucanOrchids_EN-IN1662413935_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Colour, craft and canopy life","Title":"Plate-billed mountain toucan with orchids, Ecuador","Copyright":"© Murray Cooper/Minden Pictures","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"The plate-billed mountain toucan's colourful bill features a pale yellow 'plate,' a rare trait that gives this species its name.","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260707_MountainToucanOrchids\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Plate-billed+mountain+toucan&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260706_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260707_MountainToucanOrchids"},"Ssd":"20260707","Name":"MountainToucanOrchids","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"1662413935","FullDateString":"7 Jul, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Founded by Greek settlers from Corinth around 734 BCE, the Italian city of Syracuse, on the island of Sicily, grew into one of the ancient Mediterranean's great powers and is now part of a UNESCO World Heritage Site, 'Syracuse and the Rocky Necropolis of Pantalica.' It is forever linked to Archimedes, whose genius still shapes its identity, and to Plato, who came to Syracuse hoping philosophy might shape political life. That layered past still feels tangible at Castello Maniace, a seafront fortress built for Holy Roman Emperor Frederick II in the 13th century, which can still be admired today.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.SyracuseItaly_EN-IN1535239880_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.SyracuseItaly_EN-IN1535239880_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"A city written in centuries","Title":"Syracuse, Sicily, Italy","Copyright":"© Balate Dorin/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/37.067122,15.285311/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&shading=flat&pp=37.067122,15.285311;S9;Syracuse, Sicily, Italy&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260706_SyracuseItaly\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Syracuse+Sicily&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260705_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260706_SyracuseItaly"},"Ssd":"20260706","Name":"SyracuseItaly","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"1535239880","FullDateString":"6 Jul, 2026"}],"PreloadMediaContents":[{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Perched on slender reeds, a group of barn swallows gathers in a moment of stillness that contrasts with their usual speed. Known for swift, acrobatic flight and deeply forked tails, these birds are built for life on the wing. They catch insects mid-air and travel vast distances between continents. Subtle variations in colour and markings suggest that more than one subspecies may be present, reflecting the barn swallow's extensive global range.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.HirundoRustica_EN-IN8751353148_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.HirundoRustica_EN-IN8751353148_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Wings at rest","Title":"Barn swallows of different subspecies resting together","Copyright":"© Oscar Dominguez/Tandem Stills + Motion","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"Barn swallows can travel thousands of miles between their breeding and wintering grounds each year.","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260719_HirundoRustica\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Barn+swallow&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260718_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260719_HirundoRustica"},"Ssd":"20260719","Name":"HirundoRustica","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"8751353148","FullDateString":"19 Jul, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Reflected in still water, the Rakotzbrücke—commonly known as the Devil's Bridge—forms a near-perfect stone circle in Saxony, Germany. Commissioned in 1860, the narrow basalt structure was carefully engineered so that its arch and reflection align to form a seamless ring when the lake is still. Made from locally sourced volcanic stone, it reflects precise design rather than practical function, its striking geometry intended purely for visual effect. A popular photo subject, it has also appeared in films, including 'The Matrix Resurrections' (2021). Today, the fragile bridge can only be admired from the shore, as crossing is prohibited to preserve it.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.DevilsBridge_EN-IN8517892146_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.DevilsBridge_EN-IN8517892146_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Going full circle","Title":"Devil's Bridge in Rhododendron Park Kromlau, Saxony, Germany","Copyright":"© Mike Mareen/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/51.53661,14.640453/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&shading=flat&pp=51.53661,14.640453;S9;Devil's Bridge, Kromlau, Saxony, Germany&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260718_DevilsBridge\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Devils+Bridge+Kromlau&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260717_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260718_DevilsBridge"},"Ssd":"20260718","Name":"DevilsBridge","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"8517892146","FullDateString":"18 Jul, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"On the remote northeastern tip of Crete, Greece, lies a quiet corner far from typical tourist routes. Today's image shows Vai Beach, a broad curve of golden sand bordered by calm, shallow waters of the Aegean Sea. With sunbeds, umbrellas, and showers, it's ideal for swimming, relaxing, or enjoying the peaceful atmosphere. But what truly sets Vai apart is just beyond the sand: Europe's largest natural palm grove. It consists of more than 5,000 Cretan date palm trees, a species native to Crete and parts of Turkey.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.VaiUmbrellas_EN-IN8171582034_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.VaiUmbrellas_EN-IN8171582034_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"A Greek escape","Title":"Blue sunbeds on a sandy beach in Vai, Crete, Greece","Copyright":"© borchee/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/35.30972,24.89333/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&shading=flat&pp=35.30972,24.89333;S9;Crete, Greece&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":"/maps?ty=30&q=crete%20greece&satid=id.sid%3Aa898a116-f402-c866-449a-1e49d7c0585b&vdpid=7247538364818128897&mb=36.013862~23.514471~34.598793~26.318979&cardbg=%23F98745&dt=1749198600000&tt=Crete%2C%20Crete%2C%20Greece&tsts0=%2526ty%253D30%2526q%253Dcrete%252520greece%2526satid%253Did.sid%25253Aa898a116-f402-c866-449a-1e49d7c0585b%2526vdpid%253D7247538364818128897%2526mb%253D36.013862~23.514471~34.598793~26.318979%2526cardbg%253D%252523F98745%2526dt%253D1749198600000&tstt0=Crete%2C%20Crete%2C%20Greece&cp=34.85975~13.56328&lvl=4.98&pi=0&ftst=0&ftics=False&v=2&sV=2&form=hpbal1"},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260717_VaiUmbrellas\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Crete+Greece&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260716_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260717_VaiUmbrellas"},"Ssd":"20260717","Name":"VaiUmbrellas","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"8171582034","FullDateString":"17 Jul, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"As Rath Yatra begins today, Puri, Odisha, will once again become the stage for one of India's most celebrated traditions. The festival sees Lord Jagannath, his brother Balabhadra and his sister Subhadra pulled through the streets on towering wooden chariots. The deities travel about 3 kilometres from the Jagannath Temple to Gundicha Temple, believed to be their aunt's home, where they stay for nine days.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.RathYatra2026_EN-IN7824400350_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.RathYatra2026_EN-IN7824400350_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"The wheels of tradition","Title":"The Stone Chariot, Hampi, Karnataka","Copyright":"© Alan_Lagadu/iStock/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/15.342253,76.475837/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&shading=flat&pp=15.342253,76.475837;S9;The Stone Chariot, Hampi, Karnataka&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260716_RathYatra2026\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Rath+Yatra&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260715_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260716_RathYatra2026"},"Ssd":"20260716","Name":"RathYatra2026","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"7824400350","FullDateString":"16 Jul, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"If mountains could keep a record of the past, the John Muir Wilderness near Bishop, California, United States, would have plenty to share. Its valleys, lakes and granite formations reveal a history shaped over millions of years. Established in 1964, this vast protected area spans more than 2,600 square kilometres of the Sierra Nevada and is named after naturalist John Muir. Today, parts of the Pacific Crest Trail and John Muir Trail pass through the area, drawing hikers into one of the largest high-elevation wilderness regions in the contiguous United States.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.MarieLake_EN-IN7488025421_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.MarieLake_EN-IN7488025421_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"The reward after the climb","Title":"Marie Lake, John Muir Wilderness near Bishop, California, United States","Copyright":"© Steve Dunleavy/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/36.97615,-118.812278/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&shading=flat&pp=36.97615,-118.812278;S9;John Muir Wilderness, California, United States&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260715_MarieLake\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=John+Muir+Wilderness&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260714_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260715_MarieLake"},"Ssd":"20260715","Name":"MarieLake","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"7488025421","FullDateString":"15 Jul, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"On 14 July, Shark Awareness Day asks us to trade movie panic for ocean truth. Sharks have patrolled the seas for more than 420 million years, and as apex predators, they help keep marine ecosystems in balance.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.LemonShark_EN-IN7069732478_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.LemonShark_EN-IN7069732478_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Fin-tastic truths","Title":"Lemon shark pup in mangrove forest, Eleuthera, Bahamas","Copyright":"© Shane Gross/Nature Picture Library","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"The Greenland shark can live up to 400 years, one of the longest lifespans of any vertebrate.","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260714_LemonShark\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Shark+Awareness+Day&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260713_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260714_LemonShark"},"Ssd":"20260714","Name":"LemonShark","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"7069732478","FullDateString":"14 Jul, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"International Rock Day, observed on 13 July, celebrates the geological building blocks beneath our feet and encourages curiosity about how rocks shape Earth's landscapes and history. From ancient tools to modern mineral uses, rocks hold clues to volcanic eruptions, shifting continents and the evolution of life over millions of years. In India, the vast Deccan Traps stand as a dramatic reminder of the powerful volcanic forces that have shaped our planet.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.NavajoSandstone_EN-IN8391264023_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.NavajoSandstone_EN-IN8391264023_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Born to rock","Title":"Antelope Canyon on the Navajo Nation, east of Page, Arizona, United States","Copyright":"© Mark Skalny/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/40.837774,-118.2